From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: ps4_bridge: check the DP link for fast 1080p modes

ps4_bridge_mode_valid accepts every supported CEA mode up to 297 MHz and
checks the DP link to the bridge only for 4K modes. A high-refresh monitor
offers 1080p100/120 (VIC 64/63, 297 MHz); X picks it, link training fails
("clock recovery failed") and the screen stays black (EmuFive issue #34,
CUH 9923, LG UltraGear). Run the DP link check for every mode faster than
1080p60 so modes the link cannot carry are not offered.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
@@ -126,6 +126,7 @@
 #define EDIDFIFO1 0x7c80
 #define EDID_REPLY_SKIP 3
 #define PS4_BRIDGE_MAX_CLOCK 297000
+#define PS4_BRIDGE_1080P60_CLOCK 148500
 #define PS4_BRIDGE_4K_MAX_CLOCK 594000
 #define PS4_BRIDGE_SCDC_CLOCK 340000
 #define PS4_BRIDGE_ICC_SERVICE 0x10
@@ -1438,6 +1439,11 @@ enum drm_mode_status ps4_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_connector *connector,
 		return MODE_CLOCK_HIGH;
 	if (!ps4_bridge_vic_supported(vic))
 		return MODE_BAD;
+	/* 1080p100/120 need a faster DP link to the bridge than 1080p60; offer them only when
+	 * the link can carry them, or X picks them on high-refresh monitors and link training
+	 * fails (black screen). */
+	if (mode->clock > PS4_BRIDGE_1080P60_CLOCK)
+		return amdgpu_atombios_dp_mode_valid_helper(connector, mode);
 	return MODE_OK;
 }
 
